; Jump. F on the keyboard, and Y/TRIANGLE -- button 3, "Top Action" -- because
; it is the face button the right-trigger move left empty and because BOTW,
; which is the game this project is chasing, puts jump on the top-right face
; button too (its X).
;
; IT WAS SPACE, "because Space is the jump button in every game with a
; keyboard". That is true of every game except the one this layout is now
; copying: Elden Ring puts the roll on Space and the jump on F, because in a
; game where a badly-timed roll kills you the evade gets the key you cannot
; miss. `context` took Space and this took F -- see the note there.
;
; THIS ACTION SHIPPED WITH THE ABILITY, which is the rule §4 of the contract
; states and the reason there was no `jump` here for so long: an action bound to
; nothing is a button that lies. Hero._try_start_jump, Hero._apply_gravity's
; impulse channel, and the two `ex_jump*` clips all landed in the same commit as
; these four lines.
;
; It is a real jump and not OOT's contextual ledge-hop: 0.96 m of apex, 0.59 s
; in the air, air control the whole way (K.JUMP_SPEED). Buffered, so a press
; during a fall lands and jumps; coyote-timed off the same grace the fall
; animation already used, so walking off a ledge and pressing a frame late still
; jumps. Neither is polish -- they are the two things that make a jump button
; feel like it is reading the player instead of the physics.
