; SELECT AND TALK -- A/Cross, button 0 -- AND, BEHIND A RAISED SHIELD, THE PARRY.
;
; This button has carried three other things at various points: the jump attack
; (gone to `heavy`, under the lock where OOT's Z+A lived), the dodge (gone to B,
; see `context`), and stowing a drawn item (gone to the D-pad weapon ring, which
; hands the sword back without a button that only means "undo"). What is left is
; the one thing a player at a chest, a vendor or an NPC is pressing it for --
; plus one move, on one stance.
;
; THE PARRY LIVES HERE NOW and it is gated on `shield` being held. It was
; shield+attack, and the trouble with that was not the parry, it was the SWORD:
; with the guard rewriting what RB meant, a player behind a shield could not
; swing at the thing they were guarding against without first letting the shield
; down and pressing on a later frame. A whole button of latency, charged at the
; exact moment something is about to hit you. Moving the parry off the sword
; makes RB and RT mean the same thing from every stance -- you go block -> R1 or
; block -> R2 straight through -- and puts the parry on the digit that was doing
; nothing at all behind a guard.
;
; THE TWO CLAIMS ON THIS BUTTON NEVER OVERLAP, because the stance decides and a
; guard is unambiguous: shield up, A is the parry and the world does not answer
; (`Prompt._guarding` disarms it); shield down, A is talk/open exactly as before.
; You cannot be addressing a chest and guarding against it in the same moment, so
; there is nothing here for the player to arbitrate and no rule to learn.
;
; The disarm is NOT a plain "ignore it while guarding", and the reason is worth
; the line: HeroCombat._parry drops the guard on the same tick it starts, so a
; parry press is still held for 0.62 s AFTER `shield` stops reading as blocking.
; Gate on the live stance alone and that press opens the chest as the recovery
; ends, having both parried and interacted. Prompt clears `_armed` instead, which
; only comes back on a RELEASE.
;
; A shares this button with ui_accept, which has always been safe: trade_screen's
; accept edge starts DISARMED, so the press that opens a screen cannot also
; confirm inside it. A shop is up or it is not, and the guard cannot be up while
; one is (`Prompt.blocked` gates the whole of HeroCombat's input), so the parry
; adds nothing for that arbitration to collide with.
;
; Keyboard E, which is its own key and shares nothing.
