; The kit wheel. HELD, not tapped: hold it and the eight bindings come up, point
; the RIGHT STICK or the mouse at one, and letting go is what commits it.
;
; LB -- button 9, JOY_BUTTON_LEFT_SHOULDER. CONTRACT §4 held this button empty
; "for spells" and said not to fill it because it looks empty; that reservation
; is spent here, deliberately and with the argument written down. There are no
; spells and there will not be: the three workings (GDD §6.5) are stops on the
; weapon ring, which is the decision that says this game has no casting layer.
; So the button was being kept for a system that has already been designed out,
; and the wheel has the strongest possible claim on it -- it is the left index
; finger raising a STANCE while the right hand picks out of it, which is exactly
; the pairing §4 calls the layout's spine.
;
; It does NOT collide with the shoulder that pages menu tabs. `ui_tab_prev` is
; registered at runtime by PauseMenu and only exists while the world is paused,
; where the hero reads nothing.
;
; THE KEY IS CTRL -- physical_keycode 4194326, KEY_CTRL, which on a Mac is
; Control and not Command (that is KEY_META). It is a modifier held with the
; left hand while WASD keeps working, which is the keyboard's honest translation
; of a shoulder button; every letter key near the left hand is either taken or a
; home-row raid. Holding it makes `attack` read false on plain LMB, because that
; action is read exactly (see the modifier note at the top of this block) -- and
; that is wanted rather than tolerated: the wheel is up, and swinging out of it
; would be the one press the player cannot have meant.
