; --- WHAT ELDEN RING BINDS THAT THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT --------------
;
; The keyboard layout above is Elden Ring's, minus two rows, and both are
; missing for the SAME reason rather than by oversight. CONTRACT §4: an action
; bound to nothing is a button that lies, and the fix is to ship the action with
; the ability, in one commit, not to reserve the key and hope.
;
;   CROUCH, ER's X. There is no crouch, no sneak and no stealth in this game --
;       no state, no clip, no detection rule for it to change. X is UNBOUND and
;       is being held for it: it is the key `use_item` vacated, it is where ER
;       puts crouch, and it is the only free key in the layout that is reserved
;       for a named verb rather than simply spare.
;   SKILL / ASH OF WAR, ER's Shift+RMB. LB IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY on the pad for
;       exactly this (see the D-pad note) and the keyboard matches: casting is a
;       left-hand verb, and it gets both buttons on the day it gets an ability.
;       Note that Shift+RMB would fire `shield` too if it were bound naively --
;       the guard is plain RMB, and the exact-match rule the heavy needs (see
;       `heavy`) would have to be applied to `shield` the same way.
;   MAP is G in ER and is M here, on the player's instruction. The map screen's
;       own hint prints M, Tab is the second binding, and neither moved.
